  "difficulty_reason": "H3: the complete author calculation ties weak Euler-structure torsion to a two-parameter handle-slide and exchange-point picture. It controls where exchanges occur, moves them into corner regions, uses a null-homotopic sequence of nine matrix factors to determine vertex products, then punctures the surface and compares the global products with Euler monodromy. Universal-ring rigidity identifies the winding and the root-of-unity torsion; the one-face two-fold-cover argument and full author diagrams are supplied. The positive-Euler/local-system setup is retained exactly.",
